Main use case:
Welcome screen opens: user sets his profile or pairs this device to his profile. Once profile is set up, welcome window does not show up till "Log out".
Then languages screen opens. If user already had opened some language before, then that language opens. On language's screen user can see:
  * language's panel with it's key
  * translate panel where user can search for translations
  * open conversations
  * selected poll
  * creation of new poll


There is a menu with entries:
  * Profile - opens user's profile screen where user can change nickname and avatar
  * Pairing - opens pairing screen where user can see list of paired devices, and can pair new device, revoke access for already paired device (revoke TBD)
  * Languages - opens screen with list of languages (Your languages), where user can join new language or create new own one
  * Translation API details (If language is open, activeLanguageId is set, and user is admin in opened language) - opens screen for translation API details, where user can see and edit these details
  * Language members (If language is open, activeLanguageId is set, and user is admin in opened language) - where user can see list of members and grant or remove roles for members
  * Add new translation (If language is open, activeLanguageId is set, and user has role "word creator") - where user can create new translation
  * Log out - where user's profile is removed from this device (TBD)